Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 1 18:13:52 2026 -0500

    P20 serialize an archived result once and reuse the checked bytes
    
    Before P20 the output budget check serialized the result into a counter
    and the archive writer serialized it again into a buffer. The new
    `execute_encoded` keeps the checking serialization's bytes (same admission:
    compact JSON plus a newline within the limit) and the archive writes them
    when they also fit its own limit; otherwise it falls back to the previous
    path, so every byte and every output-limit outcome is unchanged. The Python
    binding reuses the same bytes.
    
    A unit test runs both paths on 80 output budgets around the admission
    boundary, for simulate and simulate-cached, and requires identical results,
    identical bytes when admitted and exactly one serialization.
    
    The declaration gains two amendments recorded before measurement: P20 is
    judged on process time, because the work it removes ran after the core
    timer stopped, and a confirmation run checks the P13 revert.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
